  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Branded residences are most commonly associated with **luxury and upper-upscale hotel brands**, which provide the name, design standards, amenities, and often ongoing property management or hospitality services. Hotel brands represent roughly four-fifths of completed branded-residence developments globally. ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/Savills-Branded-Residences-Annual-Report-2025-2026.pdf))\n\n## Most prominent global brands\n\nAccording to Savills’ 2025/26 global leaderboard, the hotel brands with the largest completed and planned residential footprints include:\n\n1. **The Ritz-Carlton**\n2. **Four Seasons**\n3. **St. Regis**\n4. **Mandarin Oriental**\n5. **W Hotels**\n6. **Rosewood**\n7. **Fairmont**\n8. **Aman**\n9. **Autograph Collection**\n10. **Six Senses** ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/Savills-Branded-Residences-Annual-Report-2025-2026.pdf))\n\n## Common brands by hotel group\n\n| Hotel group/operator | Brands commonly used for residences |\n|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | The Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, W, EDITION, JW Marriott, The Luxury Collection, Autograph Collection |\n| **Accor** | Fairmont, Raffles, Sofitel, SLS, SO/, Mondrian, Delano |\n| **Four Seasons** | Four Seasons Private Residences |\n| **Hilton** | Waldorf Astoria, Conrad, LXR Hotels & Resorts |\n| **Hyatt** | Park Hyatt, Andaz, Thompson Hotels, The Standard, Miraval, Grand Hyatt |\n| **IHG Hotels & Resorts** | Six Senses, Regent, InterContinental, Kimpton |\n| **Banyan Group** | Banyan Tree, Angsana, Cassia |\n| **Kerzner International** | One&Only Private Homes |\n| **Mandarin Oriental Hotel Group** | The Residences at Mandarin Oriental |\n| **Rosewood Hotel Group** | Rosewood Residences |\n| **Aman Group** | Aman Residences |\n| **Kempinski** | Kempinski Residences |\n| **Minor Hotels** | Anantara Residences |\n| **Jumeirah** | Jumeirah Residences |\n| **Emaar Hospitality** | Address Residences, Vida Residences, Palace Residences |\n| **Radisson Hotel Group** | Radisson Collection and selected Radisson-branded residences |\n| **Wyndham Hotels & Resorts** | Wyndham, Registry Collection and selected upscale brands |\n\nMarriott is the largest parent group in the sector, followed by Accor; other major parent-level participants include Four Seasons, Hilton, Banyan Group, Hyatt, Radisson, IHG and Wyndham. ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/Savills-Branded-Residences-Annual-Report-2025-2026.pdf)) Hyatt specifically identifies Park Hyatt, Thompson, Andaz, The Standard and Miraval among its growing residential portfolio, while IHG operates residences under Six Senses, Regent, InterContinental and Kimpton. ([newsroom.hyatt.com](https://newsroom.hyatt.com/may-30-2025-unscriptedbyhyatt?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Practical shortlist\n\nFor a developer seeking brands with the strongest established association with branded residences, the core shortlist would normally be:\n\n**Ritz-Carlton, Four Seasons, St. Regis, Mandarin Oriental, Rosewood, Fairmont, W, Aman, Six Senses, Waldorf Astoria, Raffles, One&Only, Park Hyatt and Kempinski.**\n\nThe appropriate brand ultimately depends on the project’s positioning: **ultra-luxury** brands such as Aman or Four Seasons suit low-density premium projects, while **luxury-lifestyle** brands such as W, SLS, Andaz or Mondrian tend to suit larger urban and mixed-use developments.",
